.TH QFW-SLURM-PLUGIN.CONF 5 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-slurm-plugin.conf \- native gateway client and QPU resource mapping
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-slurm-plugin.conf
is an INI file read by the SPANK plugin, controller epilog, and standalone
driver. It defines one authenticated gateway endpoint and maps each Slurm
.B --qpu
name to one exact directory-service QPM service ID.
.PP
The file must be owned by root and must not be group- or world-writable. It
must remain readable by remote
.B slurmstepd
processes and the controller's configured
.BR SlurmUser .
.SH GATEWAY SECTION
.TP
.BI host = hostname
Gateway listener hostname or address.
.TP
.BI port = number
Gateway TCP port in the range 1 through 65535.
.TP
.BI connect_timeout_ms = milliseconds
Bound for establishing the TCP connection.
.TP
.BI request_timeout_ms = milliseconds
Absolute bound for one complete operation.
.TP
.BI max_credential_bytes = bytes
Maximum accepted MUNGE credential size.
.TP
.BI expected_munge_uid = user
Numeric UID or user name expected in gateway response credentials.
.SH RESOURCE SECTIONS
Each section has the form
.PP
.RS
.nf
[resource "nwqsim"]
service_id=nwqsim-site
.fi
.RE
.PP
The quoted section name is the public value accepted by
.BR --qpu .
The required
.B service_id
is the exact stable service ID registered by QPMd. Resource names and service
IDs must be unique and nonempty.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[gateway]
host=slurmctld
port=18095
connect_timeout_ms=5000
request_timeout_ms=120000
max_credential_bytes=65536
expected_munge_uid=qfw-slurm

[resource "nwqsim"]
service_id=nwqsim-site
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qfw-slurm/plugin.conf
Conventional installed configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/qfw-slurm/config/plugin.conf.example
Packaged example when the installation prefix is
.IR /usr .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-slurm-driver (1),
.BR qfw-slurm (7),
.BR qfw-slurm-epilog (8)
